// Package generate turns a livewire registry into its artifacts (D19): the TypeScript client
// (types.ts, filters.ts, api.ts and the copied runtime.ts and vue.ts), the OpenAPI 3.0.3
// document, the Go client package on livewire/client (D67) and the command-line client on
// github.com/urfave/cli/v3 (D68). Write is the entry point; everything it writes is
// deterministic, byte for byte, for one registry and one Options value, gofmt'ed where it is
// Go, and carries the header `Code generated by livewire. DO NOT EDIT.`.
//
// The runtime/ directory holds the TypeScript runtime sources the generator copies; they are
// tested there under bun. The Go client's runtime is the package livewire/client, which the
// generated code imports. The generator itself stays on the standard library: the generated
// CLI imports urfave/cli, the generator only writes its source.
package generate
